{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSWqAaeqqBkWyQkXvFFS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the repository. Let me summarize my findings before proceeding to design:\n\n## ANALYSIS Summary\n\n**Requirement, restated**: Implement `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED, allows idempotent retries on already-CONFIRMED shipments, rejects CANCELLED shipments with 409, and returns 404 for unknown shipments.\n\n**Repository findings**:\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`\n- ShipmentStatus enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27` (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10`\n- Error handling: via ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt`\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31`\n\n**Conventions this repository has**:\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError envelopes\n- ConflictException (409) uses ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for duplicates; ResourceNotFoundException (404) uses ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath matchers to verify status codes and error codes\n- Endpoints return ResponseEntity<T> for success, throw exceptions for errors\n- Knowledge base recommends exhaustive `when` expressions for state enums (not if/else, not when with else)\n\n**Affected files**:\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add new ErrorCode for rejected state transitions (cannot avoid: need error code for 409 case)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add POST confirm endpoint (cannot avoid: this is the feature)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for all four cases (cannot avoid: ticket requires test coverage)\n\n**Risks**:\n- Adding an ErrorCode changes the API contract; must be deliberate, not accidental\n- Idempotent retry (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED succeeds) requires careful logic\n- Without exhaustive `when` on status, a future enum value might fall through silently\n\n**Open questions**:\n- What ErrorCode name for \"cannot confirm CANCELLED shipment\"? Following SHIPMENT_* pattern, I'll use `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED`. This is not named in the ticket, but 409 Conflict requires a code from the enum, and adding it is not a dependency change.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the ErrorCode enum. This code will be thrown when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a POST endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID; if not found, throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND (404)\n   - Checks the shipment's status with exhaustive `when` expression:\n     - If CREATED: save the shipment with status CONFIRMED, return ResponseEntity.ok(updatedShipment)\n     - If CONFIRMED: return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) unchanged (idempotent)\n     - If CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - Confirms a CREATED shipment and returns CONFIRMED status\n   - Confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment and succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Rejects confirmation of a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and error code\n   - Rejects confirmation of unknown shipment with 404 and error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using if/else chain for status checks: Rejected because Kotlin's exhaustive `when` requirement (per knowledge base) provides compiler-enforced guarantees that all status values are handled. An if/else chain would compile even if a new status were added later, and a when with `else` would silently route unknown statuses to a default case.\n- Returning different HTTP status for idempotent success: Rejected because 200 OK for \"no change on retry\" is standard REST idempotency practice and simpler than checking if state changed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Via |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----|\n| CREATED → confirm | find by ID, get status | update to CONFIRMED | 200 OK, Shipment | repository.save() |\n| CONFIRMED → confirm (retry) | find by ID, get status | (none) | 200 OK, Shipment | return as-is |\n| CANCELLED → confirm | find by ID, get status | (none) | 409 Conflict, error envelope | ConflictException + GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| unknown ID → confirm | find by ID fails | (none) | 404 Not Found, error envelope | ResourceNotFoundException + GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: \"Confirms a CREATED shipment and returns CONFIRMED status\" — creates S-1 in CREATED, calls confirm, asserts 200, body.status == CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: \"Confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment and succeeds\" — creates S-2, confirms once (CONFIRMED), confirms again, asserts 200, no error\n- Test 3: \"Rejects confirmation of a CANCELLED shipment\" — manually stores S-3 in CANCELLED state, calls confirm, asserts 409, error code matches\n- Test 4: \"Rejects confirmation of unknown shipment\" — calls confirm on S-missing, asserts 404, error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":20793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10