{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSWswn3FDxNbGtvj3tKD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. The test run shows:\n- **Total tests**: 17 (all passing)\n- **ShipmentControllerTest**: 9 tests now (5 original + 4 new confirm tests)\n- **Build result**: SUCCESS\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` completed with BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — all 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass\n3. ✅ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms created shipment and persists** — test \"confirms a CREATED shipment and returns CONFIRMED status\" verifies state change; repository.save() persists it\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent** — uses same ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException pattern as existing endpoints; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelope\n5. ✅ **Repeated confirm succeeds; cancelled rejected; unknown rejected** — three separate tests cover each case with correct HTTP status (200, 409, 404) and error codes\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — only code files modified, pom.xml untouched\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — only modified ShipmentController.kt (the feature) and ApiError.kt (the required error code)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum (line 36). Required: yes, needed for 409 response code on CANCELLED shipment. Justified: follows existing ErrorCode naming pattern; adding an enum value is not a dependency change, only extends the API contract deliberately.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` endpoint (lines 59-76):\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if shipment not found (404)\n   - Uses exhaustive `when` on ShipmentStatus (required per knowledge base)\n   - CREATED → save with CONFIRMED stat